2:T608,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I choose reliable kitchen fitters in Watford?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Compare written quotations with matching scopes, check which trades are included, ask about lead times and clarify how changes or unexpected work will be handled before booking."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much do kitchen fitters charge in Watford?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"As a rough guide, straightforward fitting labour may typically be around £2,000 to £6,000, while a full renovation can cost considerably more. Every project differs, so get a free, no-obligation quote for accurate pricing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does a kitchen installation take?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"As a general guide, a simple installation may take around one to two weeks on site. Renovations involving plumbing, electrics, tiling or structural changes may take several weeks."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do kitchen fitters remove the old kitchen?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Some do and some do not. Confirm whether removal, disposal and making good are included in the quotation before work starts."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can a kitchen fitter move plumbing and electrical points?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"This may be possible, but it depends on the existing services and the proposed layout. Ask for these changes to be assessed and priced before booking."}}]}7:["slug","kitchen-fitters-watford","d"]
